    "id": "AS2BinomialDistributionProbabilityQ002",
    "moduleId": "S4",
    "topic": "Binomial Distribution",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 10,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nDennis works at a telephone-sales centre where he has to telephone members of the public and encourage them to sign up for a broadband package.\n\nOverall he has a $28\\%$ success rate.\n\nDuring each session he makes 8 calls.\n\nFind the probability that during a session Dennis has:\n\n(i) exactly 1 successful call; \\hfill [3]\n\n(ii) fewer than 3 successful calls. \\hfill [3]\n\nThe company operates a bonus scheme where operators who have 3 or more successful calls in a session are given a £50 bonus.\n\n(iii) Find Dennis's expected bonus per session. \\hfill [4]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\nLet $X$ be the random variable \"number of successful calls\".\n\n$$\nX\\sim B(8,0.28)\n$$\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | $X\\sim B(8,0.28)$ | M1 | 1 | Identifies the binomial model. |\n| 2 | $P(X=1)={}^{8}C_1(0.28)^1(0.72)^7$ | M1 | 1 | Uses the exact binomial probability formula. |\n| 3 | $P(X=1)=0.22468\\ldots=0.225\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final probability to 3 significant figures. |\n| 4 | $P(X<3)=P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2)$ | MW1 | 1 | Uses the correct cumulative expansion for fewer than 3. |\n| 5 | $P(X=0)=(0.72)^8=0.07222\\ldots$ | MW1 | 1 | Calculates the zero-success term. |\n| 6 | $P(X=2)={}^{8}C_2(0.28)^2(0.72)^6=0.3058\\ldots$ | MW1 | 1 | Calculates the two-success term and completes the sum. |\n| 7 | $P(X<3)=0.07222\\ldots+0.22468\\ldots+0.3058\\ldots=0.602728\\ldots=0.603\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | MW1 | 1 | Final cumulative probability. |\n| 8 | $P(X\\ge3)=1-P(X<3)=1-0.602728\\ldots=0.397\\ldots$ | M1, W1 | 2 | Uses the complement for 3 or more successful calls. |\n| 9 | $E(\\text{Bonus})=£50\\times P(X\\ge3)$ | M1 | 1 | Converts the bonus condition into expectation. |\n| 10 | $E(\\text{Bonus})=19.863\\ldots=£19.86$ | W1 | 1 | Final expected bonus. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n(i) $0.225$  \n(ii) $0.603$  \n(iii) $£19.86$\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nThe key step is translating the words into $X\\sim B(8,0.28)$. For the bonus, the event is $X\\ge3$, so the expected bonus is the bonus amount multiplied by that probability. Common errors include using $P(X<3)$ instead of its complement for the bonus."
