    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 7,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nAt a local airport planes cannot land if there are severe cross winds.\n\nDuring the winter months the probability of this happening on a given day is $0.04$.\n\nFind the probability that in a period of 7 winter days severe winds prevent landings on:\n\n(i) no days; \\hfill [3]\n\n(ii) 2 or more days. \\hfill [3]\n\n(iii) State why this distribution would not be suitable to calculate the probability of landing being prevented in all months of the year. \\hfill [1]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n$$\nX\\sim B(7,0.04)\n$$\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Binomial $B(7,0.04)$ | M1 | 1 | Identifies the binomial model. |\n| 2 | $P(X=0)={}^{7}C_0 0.04^0 0.96^7$ | MW1 | 1 | Uses the probability of no days with severe cross winds. |\n| 3 | $P(X=0)=0.751447\\ldots=0.751\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final probability to 3 significant figures. |\n| 4 | $P(X\\ge2)=1-P(X\\le1)=1-[P(X=0)+P(X=1)]$ | MW1 | 1 | Uses complement for 2 or more days. |\n| 5 | $P(X\\ge2)=1-[{}^{7}C_0 0.94^0 0.96^7+{}^{7}C_1 0.04^1 0.96^6]$ | M1 | 1 | Substitutes values into the complement expression. |\n| 6 | $P(X\\ge2)=1-[0.751447\\ldots+0.21917\\ldots]=1-0.9706=0.029381\\ldots=0.0294\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final upper-tail probability. |\n| 7 | Not a fixed probability of $0.04$ of success because weather is not consistent throughout the year. | MW1 | 1 | Explains why the binomial model is unsuitable all year. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n(i) $0.751$  \n(ii) $0.0294$  \n(iii) The success probability is not fixed at $0.04$ throughout the whole year because weather is not consistent throughout the year.\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nThe examiner wanted a winter-days binomial model for parts (i) and (ii), then recognition that the all-year situation breaks the constant-probability condition.\n\n### Note on Mark Scheme Transcription\n\nThe supplied mark scheme line for part (ii) appears to show ${}^{7}C_0 0.94^0 0.96^7$ in the complement expression. Since the model is $B(7,0.04)$, this has been preserved as visible mark scheme wording, but the surrounding expression and result clearly use $p=0.04$ and $q=0.96$."
