    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nWhen a biased die is thrown the probability of a score of 3 occurring is $\\frac{13}{40}$.\n\nThis die is thrown 8 times and the scores recorded.\n\nFind the probability that:\n\n(i) a score of 3 occurs exactly four times; \\hfill [3]\n\n(ii) a score of 3 occurs at most two times. \\hfill [5]\n\n(iii) Find the expected value and variance of the number of times that a score of 3 occurs. \\hfill [3]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\nLet $X$ be the random variable \"number of times 3 is scored\".\n\n$$\nX\\sim B\\left(8,\\frac{13}{40}\\right)\n$$\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | $X\\sim B\\left(8,\\frac{13}{40}\\right)$ | M1 | 1 | Identifies the binomial model. |\n| 2 | $P(X=4)={}^{8}C_4\\left(\\frac{13}{40}\\right)^4\\left(\\frac{27}{40}\\right)^4$ | MW1 | 1 | Uses the exact binomial formula. |\n| 3 | $P(X=4)=0.162\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final exact-four probability. |\n| 4 | $P(X\\le2)=P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2)$ | MW1 | 1 | Correctly interprets “at most two”. |\n| 5 | $P(X\\le2)={}^{8}C_0\\left(\\frac{13}{40}\\right)^0\\left(\\frac{27}{40}\\right)^8+{}^{8}C_1\\left(\\frac{13}{40}\\right)^1\\left(\\frac{27}{40}\\right)^7+{}^{8}C_2\\left(\\frac{13}{40}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{27}{40}\\right)^6$ | MW3 | 3 | Expands all three required terms. |\n| 6 | $P(X\\le2)=0.0431\\ldots+0.1660\\ldots+0.2797\\ldots=0.4888\\ldots=0.489\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final cumulative probability. |\n| 7 | $E(X)=np=8\\times\\frac{13}{40}=\\frac{13}{5}$ | M1 | 1 | Uses the binomial expected value formula. |\n| 8 | $E(X)=2.6$ | W1 | 1 | Final expected value. |\n| 9 | $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=npq=np(1-p)=8\\times\\frac{13}{40}\\times\\frac{27}{40}=1.755=1.76\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | MW1 | 1 | Uses the binomial variance formula. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n(i) $0.162$  \n(ii) $0.489$  \n(iii) Expected value $=2.6$, variance $=1.76$\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nThe examiner wanted correct use of $X\\sim B(8,\\frac{13}{40})$. For part (ii), all of $X=0,1,2$ must be included. For part (iii), use $np$ and $npq$."
