    "marks": 11,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nThe probability that Bob arrives late for school on any given morning is $0.35$.\n\n(i) Find the probability that in a school week he will be late exactly twice. \\hfill [3]\n\n(ii) Find the probability that in a school week he will be late at least once. \\hfill [4]\n\nBob's weekly pocket money is £10 with a deduction of £2 for each day that he is late.\n\n(iii) Find Bob's expected weekly pocket money. \\hfill [4]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\nLet $X$ be the random variable \"the number of days Bob arrives late for school\".\n\n$$\nX\\sim B(5,0.35)\n$$\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | $P(X=2)=\\binom{5}{2}(0.35)^2(0.65)^3$ | M1, MW1 | 2 | Uses the exact binomial formula for exactly twice. |\n| 2 | $P(X=2)=0.336\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final exact-two probability. |\n| 3 | $P(X\\ge1)=1-P(X=0)$ | M1, W1 | 2 | Uses complement for at least once. |\n| 4 | $P(X\\ge1)=1-(0.65)^5$ | W1 | 1 | Substitutes the probability of no late mornings. |\n| 5 | $P(X\\ge1)=1-0.11602\\ldots=0.884\\text{ (3 s.f.)}$ | W1 | 1 | Final probability. |\n| 6 | $E(X)=np=5\\times0.35=1.75$ | M1, W1 | 2 | Finds expected number of late days. |\n| 7 | $E(\\text{Deduction})=1.75\\times£2=£3.50$ | MW1 | 1 | Converts expected lateness into expected deduction. |\n| 8 | $E(\\text{Weekly pocket money})=£10-£3.50=£6.50$ | W1 | 1 | Final expected weekly pocket money. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n(i) $0.336$  \n(ii) $0.884$  \n(iii) $£6.50$\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nThe school week is treated as 5 trials with probability $0.35$ of being late each morning. For part (iii), the expected deduction is based on the expected number of late days, not on a single most likely number of late days.\n\n\n\n_No additional solution-specific diagrams._\n\n---\n# Appendix: Support Visuals and Interactive Checking Tool\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2BinomialDistributionProbabilitySupportSVG-001]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2BinomialDistributionProbabilitySupportMMD-001]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2BinomialDistributionProbabilitySupportWidget-001]\n\n# Appendix: Unmatched Mark Scheme Entries\n\nNo unmatched mark scheme entries were found in the supplied mark scheme PDF."
