    "id": "AS2ConnectedParticlesQ003",
    "moduleId": "M3",
    "topic": "Connected Particles",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 7,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nFig. 2 below shows two blocks of mass $2m\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ and $4m\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ connected by a light inextensible string which passes over a smooth fixed pulley.\n\nThe system is released from rest.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing all the external forces acting on the blocks. [2]\n\n(ii) Find the acceleration of the blocks. [5]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ003TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ003TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Force diagram: each block has tension upward and weight downward. | MW2 | 2 | Correct force diagram. |\n| 2 | $4mg-T=4ma$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Heavier block moving down. |\n| 3 | $T-2mg=2ma$. | MW1 | 1 | Lighter block moving up. |\n| 4 | $2mg=6ma$. | M1 | 1 | Add equations. |\n| 5 | $a=\\dfrac{g}{3}\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$. | W1 | 1 | Final acceleration. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`a=g/3 m s^{-2}`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nUse opposite directions of motion for the two masses and eliminate tension.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ003TikZ-002]\n\n---"
