    "id": "AS2ConnectedParticlesQ006",
    "moduleId": "M3",
    "topic": "Connected Particles",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 12,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nA block A of mass $6\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ is held at rest on a smooth plane inclined at an angle $\\theta$ to the horizontal where $\\sin\\theta=\\frac13$.\n\nIt is attached to a light inextensible string which passes over a fixed smooth light pulley to a block B of mass $m\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ which hangs freely in equilibrium as shown in Fig. 2 below.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing all the external forces acting on the two blocks. [2]\n\n(ii) Find the value of $m$. [5]\n\nBlock B is now replaced by a block C of mass $4\\,\\mathrm{kg}$. The system is released from rest and A moves up the plane.\n\n(iii) Find the acceleration of the system. [5]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ006TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ006TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Force diagram with reaction on A, tension, $6g$, and hanging weight $mg$. | MW2 | 2 | Correct external forces. |\n| 2 | For hanging block: $T=mg$. | MW1 | 1 | Equilibrium of B. |\n| 3 | For A along plane: $T=6g\\sin\\theta$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Resolves weight component on smooth plane. |\n| 4 | $mg=6g\\sin\\theta=6g(1/3)$, so $m=2$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Mass found. |\n| 5 | With $4\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ block: $4g-T=4a$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Newton’s second law for C. |\n| 6 | For A: $T-6g\\sin\\theta=6a$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Newton’s second law for A. |\n| 7 | $4g-2g=10a$, so $a=1.96\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$. | MW1 | 1 | Acceleration. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`m=2; a=1.96 m s^{-2}`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nUse equilibrium first to identify the balancing hanging mass, then use the same resolving structure for the new moving system.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ006TikZ-002]\n\n---"
