    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 11,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nFig. 5 below shows two boxes P and Q connected by a light inextensible string which passes over a smooth fixed pulley at B.\n\nAB is rough and inclined at $30^\\circ$ to the horizontal. Box P has mass $8\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ and the coefficient of friction between P and the slope AB is $0.7$. Box Q has mass $3\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ and hangs freely.\n\nThe boxes P and Q are released from rest and the string remains taut throughout the motion.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing the external forces acting on P and Q. [2]\n\n(ii) Find the magnitude of the frictional force between P and the plane AB. [3]\n\n(iii) Find the acceleration of P. [6]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ007TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ007TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Force diagram with $T$, $R$, friction, $8g$, and $3g$. | MW2 | 2 | Correct forces. |\n| 2 | Perpendicular to slope: $R=8g\\cos30^\\circ$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Normal reaction. |\n| 3 | $F_r=\\mu R=0.7(8g\\cos30^\\circ)=47.5\\,\\mathrm{N}$. | MW1 | 1 | Friction magnitude. |\n| 4 | For P: $T+8g\\sin30^\\circ-47.5=8a$. | W2 | 2 | Equation of motion as in mark scheme. |\n| 5 | For Q: $3g-T=3a$. | MW1 | 1 | Equation for hanging mass. |\n| 6 | Adding gives $21.1=11a$. | M1 | 1 | Eliminates tension. |\n| 7 | $a=1.92\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$. | W1 | 1 | Acceleration. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`F_r=47.5 N; a=1.92 m s^{-2}`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nResolve perpendicular to the plane first to get friction, then use the connected-motion equations.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ007TikZ-002]\n\n---"
