    "id": "AS2ConnectedParticlesQ008",
    "moduleId": "M3",
    "topic": "Connected Particles",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 9,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nFig. 3 below shows two particles A and B attached to the ends of a light inextensible string which passes over a smooth fixed pulley.\n\nA has mass $m_1\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ and B has mass $m_2\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ where $m_1>m_2$. Initially, A is suspended $2\\,\\mathrm{m}$ above a horizontal surface, and B is on the surface. The string is taut.\n\nThe particles are released from rest.\n\n(i) Given that the particle A hits the horizontal surface at $3\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$, find the acceleration of the system. [2]\n\n(ii) Draw a diagram showing the external forces acting on A and B. [2]\n\nWhile the string is taut, the tension in the string is $15.1\\,\\mathrm{N}$.\n\n(iii) Find $m_1$ and $m_2$. [5]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ008TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ008TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | $u=0$, $v=3$, $s=2$, use $v^2=u^2+2as$. | M1 | 1 | Find acceleration from motion of A. |\n| 2 | $9=0+2a(2)$, so $a=2.25\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$. | W1 | 1 | Acceleration. |\n| 3 | Force diagram: tension upward and weight downward for each particle. | MW2 | 2 | Correct forces. |\n| 4 | For A: $m_1g-15.1=m_1(2.25)$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Equation for heavier particle. |\n| 5 | $m_1=2$. | W1 | 1 | Mass of A. |\n| 6 | For B: $15.1-m_2g=m_2(2.25)$. | MW1 | 1 | Equation for lighter particle. |\n| 7 | $m_2=1.25$. | W1 | 1 | Mass of B. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`a=2.25 m s^{-2}; m_1=2 kg, m_2=1.25 kg`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nCombine a short SUVAT calculation with force equations using the stated tension.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ008TikZ-002]\n\n---"
