    "topic": "Connected Particles",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 14,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nFig. 1 below shows a breakdown truck of mass $1700\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ towing a car of mass $800\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ along a straight horizontal road.\n\nThe vehicles are joined by a light rigid horizontal tow bar. The truck and the car experience constant resistances to motion of magnitude $700\\,\\mathrm{N}$ and $300\\,\\mathrm{N}$ respectively. The truck’s engine produces a constant horizontal force of magnitude $2000\\,\\mathrm{N}$. Model the car and the truck as particles.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing the external forces acting on the truck and on the car. [3]\n\n(ii) Find the common acceleration of the car and the truck and the tension in the tow bar. [5]\n\nWhen the speed of the car is $8\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$, the tow bar breaks. Assume the resistance to the motion of the car remains as before.\n\n(iii) Find the distance moved by the car from the moment the tow bar breaks until the car comes to rest. [4]\n\n(ii) Find, in terms of $u$, the speed of Q immediately after the collision. [2]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ010TikZ-001]\n\nNote: The final collision line appears as an unrelated stray line at the bottom of the supplied questions PDF page. It has been preserved because it is visible in the PDF, but it does not appear to belong to this towing question.",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ010TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\nOfficial solution not found in supplied mark scheme PDF.\n\n> **Note:** Official mark scheme unavailable. Generated solution shown for study support.\n\n### Generated solution, not from official mark scheme\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Combined system: $2000-700-300=(1700+800)a$. |  |  | Uses all external horizontal forces on the two-vehicle system. |\n| 2 | $1000=2500a$, so $a=0.400\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$. |  |  | Common acceleration. |\n| 3 | Car alone: $T-300=800(0.400)$. |  |  | Tow-bar force on the car. |\n| 4 | $T=620\\,\\mathrm{N}$. |  |  | Tension in the tow bar. |\n| 5 | After tow bar breaks: $-300=800a$, so $a=-0.375\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$. |  |  | Car decelerates due to resistance only. |\n| 6 | Using $v^2=u^2+2as$: $0=8^2+2(-0.375)s$. |  |  | Stopping distance. |\n| 7 | $s=85.3\\,\\mathrm{m}$ to 3 s.f. |  |  | Generated final result. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`a=0.400 m s^{-2}; T=620 N; s=85.3 m`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nGenerated solution: use the whole system for common acceleration, isolate the car for tow-bar force, then apply SUVAT after the tow bar breaks.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ConnectedParticlesQ010TikZ-002]\n\n---"
