    "topic": "Forces & Newton's Laws",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 8,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nA particle P of mass $8\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ is being held in equilibrium on an inclined plane by a force of magnitude $55\\,\\mathrm{N}$.\n\nThe plane is smooth and inclined at an angle of $30^\\circ$ to the horizontal. The $55\\,\\mathrm{N}$ force acts at an angle $\\theta$ to the plane.\n\n(i) Complete the diagram below to show the external forces acting on P. [2]\n\n(ii) Find $\\theta$ and the magnitude of the normal reaction between the particle and the plane. [6]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ForcesNewtonsLawsQ018TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2ForcesNewtonsLawsQ018TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Completed force diagram with $R$, $55$ N force, and weight $8g$. | MW2 | 2 | Correct forces. |\n| 2 | Along plane: $8g\\sin30^\\circ=55\\cos\\theta$. | M1 M1 W1 | 3 | Equilibrium parallel to plane. |\n| 3 | $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{196}{275}$, so $\\theta=44.5^\\circ$. | W1 | 1 | Angle. |\n| 4 | Perpendicular to plane: $R=55\\sin\\theta+8g\\cos30^\\circ$. | M1 | 1 | Normal reaction. |\n| 5 | $R=106\\,\\mathrm{N}$. | W1 | 1 | Final reaction. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`theta=44.5°, R=106 N`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nOn a smooth plane there is no friction, so only the applied force, weight and normal reaction act.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2ForcesNewtonsLawsQ018TikZ-002]\n\n---"
