    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 7,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nTake $g$ to be $10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$ in this question.\n\nA lorry of mass $6000\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ is ascending a hill inclined at an angle $\\theta$ to the horizontal, where $\\sin\\theta=\\frac35$.\n\nThe resistance to the motion of the lorry is $140000\\,\\mathrm{N}$. The lorry has a deceleration of $2\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing the external forces acting on the lorry. [2]\n\n(ii) Find the tractive force produced by the lorry’s engine. [5]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2InclinedPlanesQ001TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2InclinedPlanesQ001TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Force diagram with tractive force $T$ up the plane, resistance $140000$, reaction $R$, and weight $6000g$. | MW2 | 2 | Correct external forces. |\n| 2 | $F=ma$. | M1 | 1 | Uses Newton’s second law along the slope. |\n| 3 | $T-140000-6000g\\sin\\theta=-6000(2)$. | MW3 | 3 | Includes resistance, weight component and deceleration. |\n| 4 | $T-140000-36000=-12000$. |  |  | Substitution using $g=10$, $\\sin\\theta=3/5$. |\n| 5 | $T=164000\\,\\mathrm{N}$. | W1 | 1 | Tractive force. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`T=164000 N`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nThe negative acceleration is the main sign trap: the lorry is ascending but decelerating.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2InclinedPlanesQ001TikZ-002]\n\n---"
