    "topic": "Inclined Planes",
    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 10,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nA crate of mass $30\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ rests in equilibrium on a rough plane inclined at $60^\\circ$ to the horizontal. The coefficient of friction between the crate and the plane is $\\frac13$.\n\nWhen a horizontal force, $P\\,\\mathrm{N}$, is applied to the crate it is on the point of moving up the plane, as shown in Fig. 3 below.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing all the external forces acting on the crate. [2]\n\n(ii) Find $P$. [8]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2InclinedPlanesQ003TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2InclinedPlanesQ003TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Force diagram with $P$, reaction $R$, friction $F_r$, and weight $30g$. | MW2 | 2 | Correct force diagram. |\n| 2 | Resolve up plane: $P\\cos60^\\circ=F_r+30g\\sin60^\\circ$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Equilibrium along plane. |\n| 3 | Resolve perpendicular: $R=P\\sin60^\\circ+30g\\cos60^\\circ$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Normal reaction. |\n| 4 | $F_r=\\mu R$. | M1 | 1 | Limiting friction. |\n| 5 | $\\frac12P-15g\\sqrt3=\\frac13\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}P+15g\\right)$. | M1 W2 | 3 | Combines the equations. |\n| 6 | $P=1436=1440\\,\\mathrm{N}$ to 3 s.f. | W1 | 1 | Final force. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`P=1440 N`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nBecause the crate is on the point of moving up the plane, friction acts down the plane.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2InclinedPlanesQ003TikZ-002]\n\n---"
