    "type": "Exam-Style",
    "marks": 10,
    "questionMarkdown": "### Question\n\nFig. 3 below shows a boy on a sledge being pulled by a rope up a rough slope inclined at $15^\\circ$ to the horizontal. The rope is parallel to the slope.\n\nThe boy is moving at a steady speed when the tension in the rope is $240\\,\\mathrm{N}$.\n\nThe coefficient of friction between the sledge and the slope is $\\mu$. Model the boy and the sledge as a particle of mass $50\\,\\mathrm{kg}$.\n\n(i) Draw a diagram showing all the external forces acting on the particle. [2]\n\n(ii) Find the value of $\\mu$. [8]\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2InclinedPlanesQ004TikZ-001]",
    "markSchemeMarkdown": "> See solution visual below: AS2InclinedPlanesQ004TikZ-002\n\n### Official Mark Scheme Solution\n\n| Step | Official working / result | Mark code | Mark awarded | Brief annotation |\n|---:|---|---|---:|---|\n| 1 | Force diagram with $N$, $240$, friction, and $50g$. | MW2 | 2 | Correct forces. |\n| 2 | $N=50g\\cos15^\\circ=473.30$. | M1 W1 | 2 | Resolve perpendicular to slope. |\n| 3 | $240-F_r-50g\\cos75^\\circ=0$. | M1 M1 W1 | 3 | Resolve up slope at steady speed. |\n| 4 | $F_r=113.179$. | W1 | 1 | Friction. |\n| 5 | $F_r=\\mu N$, so $113.179=473.30\\mu$. | M1 | 1 | Friction law. |\n| 6 | $\\mu=0.239$ to 3 s.f. | W1 | 1 | Coefficient. |\n\n### Final Answer\n\n`mu=0.239`\n\n### What the Examiner Wanted\n\nSteady speed means zero acceleration, so the forces balance along the slope.\n\n\n\n[VISUAL REFERENCE: AS2InclinedPlanesQ004TikZ-002]\n\n---"
